---
# Purpose
Explains the four node work settings agents read when choosing where heavy
work runs, where to set them (org, mesh, node), how inheritance works, the
defaults for your own machines, hosted nodes and guest workspaces, and the
optional local env override on a node.

# Sanitization
Written fresh from the private design (rewrite-only): no storage, service
or routing internals; only user-visible behaviour and node env names that
node owners set themselves.

# Gotchas
- Defaults must match the product (BYO always/3/note/on; hosted always/2/
  note/off; guest never/0/note/off, locked).
- Account Admin edits need a passkey check like other org/mesh/node edits.
- Org owners/admins save every level; mesh owners/admins save their mesh and
  its nodes; node owners cannot save yet (passkey check is org/mesh only).
  Update the "Who can save" table if that changes.

# Change History
- 2026-10-25: Created.
- 2026-10-25 (audit): who can save (org owners/admins only), note limits,
  the node tab's "sent to this node" list.
- 2026-10-25: "Who can save" table: mesh owners/admins can save their
  mesh and nodes; node owners not yet.
- 2026-10-29: Fifth setting Delegated turns (on|off; defaults on, guest off), separate from Heavy work; env GVMESH_NODE_DELEGATED_TURNS; fallback to Heavy work until a node reports it.
